WEBVTT

00:00:58.204 --> 00:01:02.121
The reality, however,
is a bit more complicated.

00:01:02.871 --> 00:01:07.496
A rule-based translation program
uses a lexical database,

00:01:07.538 --> 00:01:10.121
which includes all the words
you'd find in a dictionary

00:01:10.163 --> 00:01:12.163
and all grammatical forms they can take,

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:18.413
and set of rules to recognize the basic
linguistic elements in the input language.

00:01:18.454 --> 00:01:22.079
For a seemingly simple sentence 
such as “The children eat the muffins,”

00:01:22.121 --> 00:01:26.079
the program first parses its syntax,
or grammatical structure,

00:01:26.121 --> 00:01:28.663
by identifying “the children”
as the subject,

00:01:28.704 --> 00:01:30.954
and the rest of the sentence
as the predicate